<h1>Floyd-Warshall algorithm</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
An algorithm to solve the <a href="allPairsShortestPath.html"><em>all pairs shortest path</em></a> problem in a <a href="weightedDigraph.html"><em>weighted, directed graph</em></a> by multiplying an <a href="adjacencyMatrixRep.html"><em>adjacency-matrix representation</em></a> of the graph multiple times.  The edges may have negative weights, but no negative weight <a href="cycle.html"><em>cycles</em></a>. The time complexity is <a href="theta.html"><em>&Theta; (V&sup3;)</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="johnsonsAlgorithm.html"><em>Johnson's algorithm</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorSKS">SKS</a></p>

